Cryptology I
(a) Symmetric-Key encryption:
i. Classical ciphers (like Shift, Substitute, Affine, Vigen`ere, Hill) and their crypt-
analysis;
ii. Information Theoretic Security, and One-Time Pad;
iii. Pseudorandom Generators (PRG) and Stream ciphers (like CSS, RC4, Trivium,
Salsa/ChaCha); Cryptanalysis of Stream Ciphers;
iv. Pseudorandom Function (PRF) and Pseudorandom Permutation (PRP); Block
ciphers (like DES, AES); Cryptanalysis of Block ciphers;
v. Mode of Operations;
vi. Notion of CPA and CCA security with examples;
Cryptographic hash functions: Preimage, Second-Preimage and Collision resistance,
Merkle-Damgard Transform; Universal and Almost-Universal hash functions;
Symmetric-Key authentication: Message Authentication Code (MAC) (like CBC-
MAC, NMAC, HMAC), and their cryptanalysis;
Modern modes of operations: Authenticated Encryption;
Key Exchange Protocol: The Diffie-Hellman key exchange and its cryptanalysis;

